--
--   **Context.** Round six, compact controls (I2C): the correction with an abstract key program
--
--   `corrG kp B M A` is `KFL.corrRS` with the key program `keyProg` replaced by any register program
--   `kp` that pushes a key `κ k` on `rK` (`KeyOK`); the radix sort and pass 3 are the frozen ones.
--
--   **`corrG_fsp`**: for a bijection `κ` of `ℕ` (inverse `γ`) preserving `[0, M)`,
--   `flR recs M ↦ flR (recs ∘ γ) M`, at the cost `cCorrG` (moved records only in the sort).
